\section{Parameters}{

\code{Kmax} (\code{integer(1)}, required) caps model complexity: the maximum number of
changepoints (\code{label_type = "changepoint"}) or peaks (\code{label_type = "peak"})
the per-sequence segment path is searched over. The learner uses it to build
the target penalty intervals at train time and does not forward it to the
solver. Each prediction records it per sequence in its \code{extra} data
(\code{as.data.table(prediction)$Kmax}), so the label-error measure decodes the
predicted penalty under the same cap.

\code{max_depth} (\code{integer(1)}, default \code{Inf} for unlimited depth), \code{margin},
\code{n_trees} and \code{n_features} are passed to \code{\link[mmit:mmif]{mmit::mmif()}}; see there for their
meaning. \code{n_features} defaults to \code{ceiling(sqrt(p))} for \code{p} usable features
and must be at least 2. As for \link{mlr_learners_changepoint.mmit}, \code{loss} and
\code{min_sample} are not exposed because they do not change the fitted trees.

The trees are grown with \code{future.apply::future_lapply()}, so they run in
parallel under the active \code{future::plan()}. \code{future.seed = TRUE} is fixed, so
the fit is reproducible under \code{\link[=set.seed]{set.seed()}}.
}

\examples{
\dontshow{if (mlr3misc::require_namespaces(c("mmit", "future.apply", "penaltyLearning", "changepoint"), quietly = TRUE)) withAutoprint(\{ # examplesIf}
library(data.table)

set.seed(36)
signal = vector("list", 10L)
label = vector("list", 10L)
for (i in 1:10) {
  if (i \%\% 2 == 1) {
    signal[[i]] = c(rnorm(100, 18), rnorm(100, 36), rnorm(100, 9))
    label[[i]] = data.table(
      start = c(90, 190), end = c(110, 210), label = c("1change", "1change")
    )
  } else {
    signal[[i]] = rnorm(100, 0)
    label[[i]] = data.table(start = 1, end = 100, label = "0changes")
  }
}
task = TaskCpt$new(
  id = "toy", backend = data.table(signal = signal, label = label),
  target = "label", sequence = "signal", label_type = "changepoint"
)

learner = lrn("changepoint.mmif", Kmax = 3L)
\donttest{
set.seed(36)
learner$train(task)
learner$predict(task)
}
\dontshow{\}) # examplesIf}
